cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RLX in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "RLX: a small ML compiler and runtime for transformer inference and training"
abstract: >-
  RLX is an ML compiler and runtime with a JAX-shaped IR, autodiff (reverse and
  forward mode), vmap, and per-backend peak kernels for CPU, Apple Silicon
  (Metal / MLX / CoreML), NVIDIA (CUDA), AMD (ROCm), Google TPU, cross-platform
  GPU (wgpu / Vulkan / oneAPI), Qualcomm Hexagon (QNN), microcontrollers
  (Cortex-M), and FPGAs.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hauptmann
    given-names: Eugene
    affiliation: MIT
  - family-names: Kosmyna
    given-names: Nataliya
    affiliation: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/MIT-RLX/rlx"
url: "https://github.com/MIT-RLX/rlx"
license: GPL-3.0-only
version: "0.2.13"
date-released: "2026-07-18"
keywords:
  - machine learning
  - compiler
  - autodiff
  - transformer inference
  - quantization
  - heterogeneous computing
